  "reason": "The current best (config_019: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted; acc=0.639) establishes that multimodal fusion with multiprofile, avgpool aggregation, and weighted fusion is the strongest configuration so far. However, the image encoder dimension is completely unexplored — all multimodal results use resnet50, and we have zero data on imagenet_vit_l. Since the image modality contributes a meaningful ~4% gain in the multimodal setting (config_016 vs config_001), a stronger image encoder could provide a larger complementary signal. Config_025 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings at the current best, giving a clean A/B comparison that isolates the image-encoder effect. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact untested dimension, making it the most informative use of the next experiment under a limited budget."
}

